# Security policy

Do not report a suspected vulnerability in a public issue, discussion or pull request.

## Reporting a vulnerability

**Use GitHub private vulnerability reporting.** On this repository's
[Security tab](https://github.com/{{packageName}}/security/policy), choose
*Report a vulnerability*. The report arrives attached to the repository, with a
draft advisory and a CVE request path in place. It is off by default, so switch
it on once the repository is public, and keep naming it here only while the
button is there:

```bash
gh api -X PUT repos/{{packageName}}/private-vulnerability-reporting
```

**Or email [security@simtabi.com](mailto:security@simtabi.com).** That is the only
disclosure address, and it works whether or not the button is available. Other
Simtabi addresses, including `ichava@simtabi.com`, handle community mail and
may delay a report.

Response times, coordinated disclosure, safe harbor and credit follow the
[organisation security policy](https://github.com/ichava/.github/blob/main/SECURITY.md).

## Scope

This package ships icon assets and the provider that registers them with
`ichava/core`.

Core owns sanitisation, caching, seeding and the HTTP surface, so a defect in
how an icon is sanitised, cached or served belongs to
[ichava/core](https://github.com/ichava/core) rather than here. What belongs
here is the vendored assets themselves, this package's own registration code,
and anything in its build or sync tooling that widens what a refresh can reach.
